Aha! In 'scare' mode, animateAnimatronic sets `model.position.x = sin*...` and `model.position.y = sin*...` **every frame**, overriding the y position we set (-2.7) with ±0.02! Yes! The model position is overwritten by the scare animation to near 0 (camera eye level y≈0), which puts the character's head at local y=2.74 above camera center, while the feet at y≈0 are at eye level. That's exactly why we see feet at eye level. The original position set in startScare is immediately overwritten each frame by animateAnimatronic mode 'scare'. So the fix belongs in models.js: the scare animation should only jitter around the base position, not reset y to 0. Or startScare should not set y, but instead the animation should preserve base. Easiest: in animateAnimatronic scare mode, store a base or only apply jitter in z? The model.position is the root's local position relative to camera. We need y=-2.7 preserved. Change:

