Both modals fit, but the bottom content of night select/handbook is cut off at the modal card bottom (we can see partial text clipped at bottom edge; the card is scrollable). For the night select, the "PLAY NIGHT 1" button is not visible, requiring scroll. That's poor UX on landscape mobile. Similarly how-to modal footer/buttons cut off. The modal card max-height 92svh with overflow auto, so scrollable but the primary action hidden. On a 390px tall landscape phone, a user might not realize to scroll. We should improve landscape modal layout to fit or make scroll obvious.

The night select card height 483? Our earlier measurement for settings 483 vs 357. For night select maybe ~? It shows 2 rows plus header, but play button and note below cut. We should compact modals in landscape (max-height 600) with smaller header/buttons and possibly 3 columns already. At 844 wide, night grid is 3 cols, so height should be header ~100 + 2 rows * 105 + gaps + note/button ~90 = 400+. Can't fit 390. Options:
- reduce header margin/font
- reduce night button min-height to 70
- hide modal-note in landscape
- make card padding smaller
- place play button sticky at bottom? Better: compact enough to fit.

For how-to: help grid items each ~115, 2 rows = 230 + header 80 + footer 50 + buttons 48 -> 408. Reduce help icon sizes and text, hide foot or make compact, reduce header margin, smaller button. Could still fit around 350.

